node_modules/
.env
__pycache__/

# Trained artefacts are ignored by default - they are build output, and an
# experiment's throwaway .pkl has no business in the history.
*.pkl

# model.pkl is the exception, and it has to be. It is the only artefact the
# service actually serves: /predict returns 500 "Model not trained yet" without
# it. While it was ignored it never reached a checkout or a container image, so
# the backend silently fell back to its hand-written difficulty heuristic and
# the Random Forest never ran in the product at all.
!model.pkl
